{"parentUuid":"b8162334-870b-4b2b-a62b-85c8e340e5f3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011Jx6xJxqYwkGUJ2pvSJs4c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looked at the shape. Good news: the per-agent schema knowledge we need already exists — it lives in `cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/` as one file per agent (`codex.go` 467 LOC, `gemini.go` 263, `opencode.go` 220, `copilot.go` 248, `droid.go` 99, plus the dispatcher `compact.go` with format sniffers `isCodexFormat` / `isOpenCodeFormat` / …). Each compactor already knows exactly where content lives — e.g. OpenCode's `emitOpenCodeAssistant` reaches into `parts[].text`, `parts[].state.input`, `parts[].state.output`; Codex pulls from `payload.content`, `payload.arguments`, `payload.output`. **That's the same knowledge a content-targeted redactor needs**, just consumed differently.\n\nThe clean shape isn't a new `ContentSpans` method bolted onto `TranscriptCompactor` — it's one level deeper. Each agent file should expose a **content visitor**:\n\n```go\ntype ContentKind int\nconst (\n    KindUserText ContentKind = iota\n    KindAssistantText\n    KindToolInput\n    KindToolOutput\n    KindMetadata     // ids, paths, timestamps — skip or shallow-scan only\n)\n\ntype Visitor interface {\n    OnString(kind ContentKind, value string)\n}\n\n// each agent implements:\ntype TranscriptParser interface {\n    Format() string\n    Sniff(raw []byte) bool\n    Walk(raw []byte, v Visitor) error\n}\n```\n\nThen both `compact*` and `redactContent*` become consumers of the same visitor — compaction emits transcript lines, redaction runs detectors at low entropy on `User/Assistant/Tool*` strings and skips `Metadata` entirely. No more allowlist-of-keys-to-skip; structural fields are unreachable by construction. This is also the clean OSS surface — the visitor interface, the generic detector core, and the per-agent parsers are all the package needs to expose.\n\n**Tradeoff is real**: it's a refactor of ~1,900 LOC of existing compactor code, not a small change. I'd stage it: introduce the visitor + port droid (99 LOC, simplest), prove it produces byte-identical compact output via the existing test fixtures, then port one agent per PR. Roughly 4–6 PRs of work.\n\nWant me to write that up as a design doc / plan, or prototype the visitor against droid first to confirm the abstraction holds before committing to the refactor?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1194,"cache_read_input_tokens":106091,"output_tokens":2655,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1194,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2655,"cache_read_input_tokens":106091,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1194},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cavq7tjUXqURxvR1anrDW","type":"assistant","uuid":"6189815c-76de-4203-b18a-73822543e4ec","timestamp":"2026-05-11T13:06:12.357Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"c277888e-b12d-4ae6-bfa7-0736750a0659","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/improve-redaction"}
