{"parentUuid":"cd47a24c-041f-4d7d-9c79-25b06ef04eb3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Gxw8QpXurVhA8o5nYt9qCc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prototype is in `redact/agent/` — 323 LOC of code + 189 of tests, all three tests passing, lint clean.\n\n## What's there\n\n**`visitor.go`** — the interface. A `Walker` is just `func(raw []byte, v Visitor) error`. `Visitor.OnString(kind, value)` receives every content-bearing string tagged with one of `KindUserText` / `KindAssistantText` / `KindToolName` / `KindToolInput` / `KindToolOutput`. No metadata kind exists by design — structural fields are simply not emitted.\n\n**`claudecode.go`** — `WalkClaudeCode` parses each JSONL line, reaches into `message.content`, and emits *only* content strings. `tool_use.input` is walked recursively because tool argument schemas are arbitrary. `thinking` text is emitted as assistant text; the high-entropy `signature` field beside it is **not**, which directly fixes the kind of false-positive the current allowlist relies on `skip` keys to avoid.\n\n**`redactor.go`** — `Redact(walk, raw, scan)` runs the walker with a collecting visitor, deduplicates values, runs `scan` (defaults to `redact.String`, but pluggable — that's the seam for the lower entropy threshold), and applies replacements as JSON-encoded string substitutions over the raw bytes. Byte-identical output when nothing matched.\n\n## What the three tests prove\n\n1. **`TestWalkClaudeCode_EmitsContentOnly`** — feeds a real-shaped Claude Code line with planted uuids, promptId, sessionId, requestId, msg ids, tool_use_id, signature, model name, timestamp, cwd, gitBranch. Asserts every piece of content is visited AND that every one of those structural values is *not*. This is the structural guarantee — false positives on UUIDs/signatures/paths become impossible because the redactor never sees them.\n\n2. **`TestRedact_ScansOnlyContent`** — plants a high-entropy AWS-style secret in user text, an Anthropic-style bearer token in a `Bash` tool's `command` arg, and a credentialed Postgres URI in tool output. All three get redacted. UUIDs/ids in the same lines survive untouched.\n\n3. **`TestRedact_LowThresholdCatchesLowEntropySecret`** — plants `password123password123` (entropy ~3.4, well below the current 4.5 threshold). The current generic redactor misses it. By passing a custom `ScanFunc` that adds a low-entropy heuristic, the content-only redactor catches it — and because it only ever sees content strings, the more aggressive heuristic carries zero risk to structural fields.\n\n## What this validates\n\n- The visitor abstraction generalises (Claude Code's nested `tool_use.input` was the trickiest schema feature I could think of, and it dropped out as a generic recursive walk).\n- \"Content positive\" is a structural property, not a discipline — even with a much more aggressive scanner, you can't false-positive on a UUID because the scanner is never asked about it.\n- The scanning policy (entropy threshold, betterleaks rules, custom heuristics) is fully decoupled from where content lives. Each agent owns only its schema.\n\n## What this prototype deliberately doesn't do\n\n- No second agent — the next worthwhile step is porting one more (probably droid, since it's 99 LOC and would tell us whether the visitor needs richer events for chunked/streaming shapes).\n- No `compact` wiring — the bigger payoff is folding compaction into the same visitor so both consumers share one parser per agent, but that's a real refactor (1,900+ LOC of existing compact code).\n- No tuned low-entropy `ScanFunc` — test 3 uses a contrived `Contains(\"password\")` heuristic just to demonstrate the seam. The real version would thread an entropy threshold parameter into `redact.String`.\n\nFiles:\n- `redact/agent/visitor.go:1`\n- `redact/agent/claudecode.go:1`\n- `redact/agent/redactor.go:1`\n- `redact/agent/claudecode_test.go:1`\n\nWant me to port droid next as the second proof point, or hold here and write up the design as a doc you can review/share?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180,"cache_read_input_tokens":143592,"output_tokens":1416,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":180,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":143592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":180},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CavxXjfFoYLqeA7jqj4yQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"fff9029c-f97e-4ba1-8917-0e4d8f09a8d7","timestamp":"2026-05-11T14:43:07.300Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"c277888e-b12d-4ae6-bfa7-0736750a0659","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/improve-redaction"}
