d on it, but that change is bigger than the helper.\n\n3. **`bufio.NewReader(...).ReadBytes('\\n')` loop in `WalkClaudeCode`** vs existing JSONL iterators\n   - The same loop shape appears in `cmd/entire/cli/transcript/parse.go:17` (`ParseFromBytes`), `compact/compact.go:286` (`parseJSONLEntries`), `compact/codex.go:199`, and `compact/copilot.go:81`. There is **no** shared `IterateJSONLines(b, fn)` helper today — every caller open-codes the same loop.\n   - Verdict: **DUPLICATE-ACCEPTABLE on this branch, but flag as an existing wart.** The new file is the 5th instance, so the cost of inlining once more is low; the cleanup is a separate refactor that should extract a `transcript.IterateLines(content, func(line []byte) error)` helper used by all five sites.\n\n4. **`walkAny` (recursive JSON walker over `tool_use.input`)** vs `collectJSONLReplacements` in `redact/redact.go`\n   - Both walk a parsed `any` tree across `map[string]any` / `[]any` / `string`. But `collectJSONLReplacements` is doing materially more work: tracking the parent key, propagating `credentialContext`, consulting `shouldSkipJSONLField` / `shouldSkipJSONLObject` / `isCredentialJSONSecretKey`, and emitting `jsonReplacement` records keyed by field name. `walkAny` emits every string with a single `Kind` and explicitly does not need any of that — the walker's entire premise is that the *caller* picked these strings as content.\n   - Verdict: **NOT-A-DUPLICATE.** Shapes overlap, but the semantics are different and merging them would re-introduce exactly the key-based heuristic the prototype is trying to delete.\n\n5. **`head.Type` switch on `\"user\"`/`\"human\"`/`\"assistant\"`** vs `normalizeKind` in `compact/compact.go`\n   - `compact.normalizeKind` already canonicalises `user`/`human`/role-based variants into `transcript.TypeUser`/`TypeAssistant` and uses the shared `transcript.TypeUser` / `TypeAssistant` / `userAliases` constants. The new code re-hardcodes the alias set in a switch.\n   - However, `normalizeKind` is package-private to `compact`, it consults `droppedTypes` (compact-specific filtering), and it operates on a pre-parsed `map[string]json.RawMessage`. Reusing it requires either exporting it or pulling it down to `cmd/entire/cli/transcript/`.\n   - Verdict: **DUPLICATE-ACCEPTABLE for the prototype, REUSE for landing.** At minimum, the new code should reference `transcript.TypeUser` / `transcript.TypeAssistant` constants (already in `cmd/entire/cli/transcript/types.go`) instead of bare `\"user\"`/`\"assistant\"` string literals. Promoting the alias logic into a shared `transcript.NormalizeKind` is the right follow-up so both compact and the redactor share one definition of \"what counts as a user message.\"\n\n### Net recommendation\n\nThe clearest win is **Finding 1**: `encodeJSONString` + the dedupe/replace loop is a direct rebuild of helpers that already exist in the same `redact/` package. Wire `redact/transcript/redactor.go` through `redact.jsonEncodeString` + `redact.applyJSONReplacements` and drop the local copies. Findings 2, 3, and 5 are real duplication but each requires moving a helper across a package boundary — fine to file as a follow-up cleanup rather than block the prototype. Finding 4 is not duplication."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a64826bee46fb6978 (use SendMessage with to: 'a64826bee46fb6978' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 69497\ntool_uses: 8\nduration_ms: 50702</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"3384c56e-f158-4cfb-b269-e43fbb39eda2","timestamp":"2026-05-11T15:33:29.645Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are doing a code-reuse review of a prototype on branch `soph/improve-redaction` in /Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli.\n\nThe full diff is at /tmp/simplify-diff.txt — read it first.\n\nContext: We're prototyping a content-targeted transcript redaction library. The library lives at `redact/transcript/` (`visitor.go`, `redactor.go`, `claudecode.go` + test). It exposes a `Visitor` / `Walker` / `Redact` API. A 