ves (good) but might also drop *less-aggressive* matches in places the old whole-file scan caught accidentally (need to verify each removal is safe)\n\n**The blocker**: only Claude Code and Codex have walkers right now. Gemini, OpenCode, Copilot CLI, Factory Droid, Cursor would all fall back to `redact.JSONLBytes` until ported. That's fine for incremental rollout (each agent flips independently as its walker lands), but if you want the flag on by default for everyone, that's 4–5 more walkers first. Cursor and Factory Droid use the same Anthropic message shape as Claude Code, so they might be near-free; OpenCode (single-JSON-object) and Gemini (its own shape) are real ports.\n\n**Main risk**: differential output. The new path's \"smaller scan surface\" is a feature for UUIDs/signatures, but if any of the existing call-site fixtures or integration tests pin specific redacted output bytes, those will need updating. I'd grep for `REDACTED` in `**/*_test.go` first to size that surface.\n\nWant me to draft the helper + flag-gated wiring as one focused PR (just claude-code + codex + flag, default off), or write up the differential-testing plan first so we know what we're risking before touching the hot path?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":273660,"output_tokens":3963,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1007,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3963,"cache_read_input_tokens":273660,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1007,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1007},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaxRGcUtR6ZK3XsCUAPcd","type":"assistant","uuid":"146af24e-c3b0-4b8b-b7a9-df2b291234a4","timestamp":"2026-05-12T09:14:48.241Z","userType":